IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cb2-nouns`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), Part VII, sections 76 to 81 -- REGISTRATION OF A
-- TRANSFER: the issuer's duty to register, the assurance it may require, its duty to inquire into adverse
-- claims, its limited liability, lost or stolen securities, and its agents. Layer 1.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Encoded from a plain-text rendering of the Justice Canada consolidation current to
-- 2026-09-30, which is not an official version; nothing here is verified against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RULE. Named `<what it works out> within s <section>`. Where a provision says what follows in
-- a stated case, the rule is TRUE when that case holds; FALSE means only that this provision does not apply.
-- A rule whose result is a MAYBE returns NOTHING where the text is silent for the case.
-- Within this module a rule that depends on another section's rule calls it and takes its inputs, as long as
-- the callee asks for no more than eight facts; where it would carry more (s 78(1) with s 78(2), and the
-- rules for s 78(3)), the caller takes the callee's RESULT as a plain input named for it, and says so.
-- Across modules a plain input stands in for the other rule's result and the comment names the rule that
-- works it out: the rules for s 65 take eleven facts about the endorser, and those for s 52 and s 49(2) are
-- in other modules.

§ `s 76 Registration`

§§ `s 76(1) Duty to register transfer`

-- The issuer shall register the transfer "if" (a) to (f). Read as: the duty arises when all six hold;
-- FALSE means only that s 76(1) imposes no duty, not that the issuer may not register.
-- (a) is the result of `the person is an appropriate person within s 65(1)` in cb2-part7-endorsement.l4.
-- (f): TRUE where no fee is charged.
-- (c) "no duty to inquire into adverse claims or has discharged any such duty" is worked out by the rule
-- `the issuer had no duty to inquire into adverse claims or had discharged any such duty within s 78(1)` below.
-- src:1018 | 76 (1) Where a security in registered form is presented for transfer, the issuer shall register the transfer if
-- src:1019 | (a) the security is endorsed by an appropriate person as defined in section 65;
-- src:1020 | (b) reasonable assurance is given that that endorsement is genuine and effective;
-- src:1021 | (c) the issuer has no duty to inquire into adverse claims or has discharged any such duty;
-- src:1022 | (d) any applicable law relating to the collection of taxes has been complied with;
-- src:1023 | (e) the transfer is rightful or is to a bona fide purchaser; and
-- src:1024 | (f) any fee referred to in subsection 49(2) has been paid.
@ref CBCA s 76(1) (src:1018-1024)
GIVEN `a security in registered form is presented for transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the security is endorsed by an appropriate person as defined in section 65` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reasonable assurance is given that the endorsement is genuine and effective` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the issuer has a duty to inquire into adverse claims` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the issuer has discharged any duty to inquire into adverse claims` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any applicable law relating to the collection of taxes has been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transfer is rightful` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transfer is to a bona fide purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any fee referred to in subsection 49(2) has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the issuer must register the transfer within s 76(1)` MEANS
        `a security in registered form is presented for transfer`
    AND `the security is endorsed by an appropriate person as defined in section 65`
    AND `reasonable assurance is given that the endorsement is genuine and effective`
    AND `the issuer had no duty to inquire into adverse claims or had discharged any such duty within s 78(1)`
            `the issuer has a duty to inquire into adverse claims`
            `the issuer has discharged any duty to inquire into adverse claims`
    AND `any applicable law relating to the collection of taxes has been complied with`
    AND (   `the transfer is rightful`
         OR `the transfer is to a bona fide purchaser`)
    AND `any fee referred to in subsection 49(2) has been paid`

§§ `s 76(2) Liability for delay`

-- The issuer is "liable to the person presenting it for registration for loss resulting from any
-- unreasonable delay in registration or from failure or refusal to register the transfer". The answer is the
-- amount of that loss. NOTHING: the issuer has no duty to register, or there was no unreasonable delay,
-- failure or refusal.
-- src:1025 | Liability for delay
-- src:1026 | (2) Where an issuer has a duty to register a transfer of a security, the issuer is liable to the person presenting it for registration for loss resulting from any unreasonable delay in registration or from failure or refusal to register the transfer.
@ref CBCA s 76(2) (src:1025-1026)
GIVEN `a security in registered form is presented for transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the security is endorsed by an appropriate person as defined in section 65` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reasonable assurance is given that the endorsement is genuine and effective` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the issuer has a duty to inquire into adverse claims` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the issuer has discharged any duty to inquire into adverse claims` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any applicable law relating to the collection of taxes has been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transfer is rightful` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transfer is to a bona fide purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any fee referred to in subsection 49(2) has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the issuer unreasonably delays the registration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the issuer fails or refuses to register the transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the loss resulting from the delay, failure or refusal in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the issuer's liability to the person presenting the security in dollars within s 76(2)` MEANS
    IF     `the issuer must register the transfer within s 76(1)`
               `a security in registered form is presented for transfer`
               `the security is endorsed by an appropriate person as defined in section 65`
               `reasonable assurance is given that the endorsement is genuine and effective`
               `the issuer has a duty to inquire into adverse claims`
               `the issuer has discharged any duty to inquire into adverse claims`
               `any applicable law relating to the collection of taxes has been complied with`
               `the transfer is rightful`
               `the transfer is to a bona fide purchaser`
               `any fee referred to in subsection 49(2) has been paid`
       AND (   `the issuer unreasonably delays the registration`
            OR `the issuer fails or refuses to register the transfer`)
    THEN JUST `the loss resulting from the delay, failure or refusal in dollars`
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `s 77 Assurance that endorsement effective`

§§ `s 77(1) Assurance that endorsement effective`

-- src:1028 | 77 (1) An issuer may require an assurance that each necessary endorsement on a security is genuine and effective by requiring a guarantee of the signature of the person endorsing, and by requiring
-- src:1029 | (a) if the endorsement is by an agent or mandatary, reasonable assurance of authority to sign;
-- src:1030 | (b) if the endorsement is by a fiduciary, evidence of appointment or incumbency;
-- src:1031 | (c) if there is more than one fiduciary, reasonable assurance that all who are required to sign have done so; and
-- src:1032 | (d) in any other case, assurance that corresponds as closely as practicable to the foregoing.
@ref CBCA s 77(1) (src:1028-1032)
DECLARE `Requirement an issuer may make under s 77(1)` IS ONE OF
    `a guarantee of the signature of the person endorsing`
    `reasonable assurance of authority to sign`
    `evidence of appointment or incumbency`
    `reasonable assurance that all who are required to sign have done so`
    `an assurance that corresponds as closely as practicable to the foregoing`

-- The guarantee of the signature may always be required. Paragraphs (a) to (c) add one requirement each; (d)
-- applies "in any other case", which is read as: the endorsement is neither by an agent or mandatary nor by
-- a fiduciary (fork F-P7-12).
-- src:1028 | 77 (1) An issuer may require an assurance that each necessary endorsement on a security is genuine and effective by requiring a guarantee of the signature of the person endorsing, and by requiring
-- src:1029 | (a) if the endorsement is by an agent or mandatary, reasonable assurance of authority to sign;
-- src:1030 | (b) if the endorsement is by a fiduciary, evidence of appointment or incumbency;
-- src:1031 | (c) if there is more than one fiduciary, reasonable assurance that all who are required to sign have done so; and
-- src:1032 | (d) in any other case, assurance that corresponds as closely as practicable to the foregoing.
@ref CBCA s 77(1) (src:1028-1032)
GIVEN `the endorsement is by an agent or mandatary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the endorsement is by a fiduciary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is more than one fiduciary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Requirement an issuer may make under s 77(1)`
`what the issuer may require within s 77(1)` MEANS
    append (LIST `a guarantee of the signature of the person endorsing`)
           (append `the agent requirement, if any`
                   (append `the fiduciary requirement, if any`
                           (append `the several fiduciaries requirement, if any` `the other case requirement, if any`)))
    WHERE
        `the agent requirement, if any` MEANS
            IF `the endorsement is by an agent or mandatary` THEN LIST `reasonable assurance of authority to sign` ELSE EMPTY
        `the fiduciary requirement, if any` MEANS
            IF `the endorsement is by a fiduciary` THEN LIST `evidence of appointment or incumbency` ELSE EMPTY
        `the several fiduciaries requirement, if any` MEANS
            IF `there is more than one fiduciary` THEN LIST `reasonable assurance that all who are required to sign have done so` ELSE EMPTY
        `the other case requirement, if any` MEANS
            IF NOT (`the endorsement is by an agent or mandatary` OR `the endorsement is by a fiduciary`)
            THEN LIST `an assurance that corresponds as closely as practicable to the foregoing`
            ELSE EMPTY

§§ `s 77(2) Definition of guarantee of the signature`

-- src:1033 | Definition of guarantee of the signature
-- src:1034 | (2) For the purposes of subsection (1), a guarantee of the signature means a guarantee signed by or on behalf of a person reasonably believed by the issuer to be responsible.
@ref CBCA s 77(2) (src:1033-1034)
GIVEN `the guarantee is signed by or on behalf of a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the issuer reasonably believes that person to be responsible` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`guarantee of the signature within s 77(2)` MEANS
        `the guarantee is signed by or on behalf of a person`
    AND `the issuer reasonably believes that person to be responsible`

§§ `s 77(3) Standards`

-- src:1035 | Standards
-- src:1036 | (3) An issuer may adopt reasonable standards to determine responsible persons for the purpose of subsection (2).
@ref CBCA s 77(3) (src:1035-1036)
GIVEN `the standards are reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the issuer may adopt the standards to determine responsible persons within s 77(3)` MEANS
    `the standards are reasonable`

§§ `s 77(4) Definition of evidence of appointment or incumbency`

-- (a) For a fiduciary appointed by a court: a copy of the order certified in accordance with subsection 51(7)
-- (out of range of the rules in this module: the certifying is s 51(7), in cb2-part7-registers.l4, so it is a
-- plain input), dated not earlier than sixty days before the date the security is presented for transfer.
-- (b) In any other case: a copy of a document showing the appointment, or other evidence the issuer believes
-- appropriate.
-- src:1037 | Definition of evidence of appointment or incumbency
-- src:1038 | (4) In paragraph (1)(b), evidence of appointment or incumbency means
-- src:1039 | (a) in the case of a fiduciary appointed by a court, a copy of the order certified in accordance with subsection 51(7), and dated not earlier than sixty days before the date a security is presented for transfer; or
-- src:1040 | (b) in any other case, a copy of a document showing the appointment or other evidence believed by the issuer to be appropriate.
@ref CBCA s 77(4) (src:1037-1040)
GIVEN `the fiduciary was appointed by a court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is a copy of the order certified in accordance with subsection 51(7)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the order` IS A DATE
      `the date the security is presented for transfer` IS A DATE
      `the document is a copy of a document showing the appointment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is other evidence the issuer believes to be appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`evidence of appointment or incumbency within s 77(4)` MEANS
    IF `the fiduciary was appointed by a court`
    THEN     `the document is a copy of the order certified in accordance with subsection 51(7)`
         AND `the date of the order` AT LEAST (`the earliest day allowed by` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 60, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `counted back from` `the date the security is presented for transfer`)
    ELSE     `the document is a copy of a document showing the appointment`
          OR `the document is other evidence the issuer believes to be appropriate`

§§ `s 77(5) Standards`

-- src:1041 | Standards
-- src:1042 | (5) An issuer may adopt reasonable standards with respect to evidence for the purposes of paragraph (4)(b).
@ref CBCA s 77(5) (src:1041-1042)
GIVEN `the standards are reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the issuer may adopt the standards for evidence under paragraph 77(4)(b) within s 77(5)` MEANS
    `the standards are reasonable`

§§ `s 77(6) No notice to issuer`

-- The issuer is deemed not to have notice of the contents of a document referred to in (4) "except to the
-- extent that the contents relate directly to appointment or incumbency". JUST FALSE: deemed not to have
-- notice. NOTHING: s 77(6) says nothing, because the document is not one referred to in (4) or the contents
-- relate directly to appointment or incumbency.
-- src:1043 | No notice to issuer
-- src:1044 | (6) An issuer is deemed not to have notice of the contents of any document referred to in subsection (4) except to the extent that the contents relate directly to appointment or incumbency.
@ref CBCA s 77(6) (src:1043-1044)
GIVEN `the document is a document referred to in subsection 77(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contents relate directly to appointment or incumbency` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the issuer has notice of the contents within s 77(6)` MEANS
    IF     `the document is a document referred to in subsection 77(4)`
       AND (NOT `the contents relate directly to appointment or incumbency`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 77(7) Notice from excess documentation`

-- src:1045 | Notice from excess documentation
-- src:1046 | (7) If an issuer demands assurance additional to that specified in this section for a purpose other than that specified in subsection (4) and obtains a copy of a will, trust or partnership agreement, by-law or similar document, the issuer is deemed to have notice of all matters contained therein affecting the transfer.
@ref CBCA s 77(7) (src:1045-1046)
GIVEN `the issuer demands assurance additional to that specified in section 77 for a purpose other than that specified in subsection 77(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the issuer obtains a copy of a will, trust or partnership agreement, by-law or similar document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the issuer is deemed to have notice of all matters contained in the document affecting the transfer within s 77(7)` MEANS
        `the issuer demands assurance additional to that specified in section 77 for a purpose other than that specified in subsection 77(4)`
    AND `the issuer obtains a copy of a will, trust or partnership agreement, by-law or similar document`

§ `s 78 Limited duty of inquiry`

§§ `s 78(4) Duration of notice`

-- A written notice of adverse claim is effective for twelve months from the date it was received unless it is
-- renewed in writing. A renewal restarts the twelve months (fork F-P7-9); the caller passes a renewal only if
-- it was made while the notice was still effective.
-- src:1060 | Duration of notice
-- src:1061 | (4) A written notice of adverse claim received by an issuer is effective for twelve months from the date when it was received unless the notice is renewed in writing.
@ref CBCA s 78(4) (src:1060-1061)
GIVEN `the date the written notice was received` IS A DATE
      `the date the written notice was last renewed in writing, if it was` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the written notice of adverse claim is effective within s 78(4)` MEANS
        `done within the time limit` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 12, `unit of time` IS `calendar months`) `the date the written notice was received` `the day asked about`
    OR  CONSIDER `the date the written notice was last renewed in writing, if it was`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST r THEN `done within the time limit` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 12, `unit of time` IS `calendar months`) r `the day asked about`

§§ `s 78(1) Limited duty of inquiry`

-- src:1047 | Limited duty of inquiry
-- src:1048 | 78 (1) An issuer to whom a security is presented for registration has a duty to inquire into adverse claims if
-- src:1049 | (a) written notice of an adverse claim has been received at a time and in a manner that affords the issuer a reasonable opportunity to act on it before the issue of a new, reissued or re-registered security and the notice discloses the name and address of the claimant, the registered owner and the issue of which the security is a part; or
-- src:1050 | (b) the issuer is deemed to have notice of an adverse claim from a document that it obtained under subsection 77(7).
@ref CBCA s 78(1) (src:1047-1050)
GIVEN `written notice of an adverse claim has been received at a time and in a manner that affords the issuer a reasonable opportunity to act on it before the issue of a new, reissued or re-registered security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice discloses the name and address of the claimant, the registered owner and the issue of which the security is a part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the written notice was received` IS A DATE
      `the date the written notice was last renewed in writing, if it was` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
      `the issuer demands assurance additional to that specified in section 77 for a purpose other than that specified in subsection 77(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the issuer obtains a copy of a will, trust or partnership agreement, by-law or similar document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matters contained in the document include an adverse claim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the issuer has a duty to inquire into adverse claims within s 78(1)` MEANS
        (    `written notice of an adverse claim has been received at a time and in a manner that affords the issuer a reasonable opportunity to act on it before the issue of a new, reissued or re-registered security`
         AND `the notice discloses the name and address of the claimant, the registered owner and the issue of which the security is a part`
         AND `the written notice of adverse claim is effective within s 78(4)`
                 `the date the written notice was received`
                 `the date the written notice was last renewed in writing, if it was`
                 `the day asked about`)
    OR  (    `the issuer is deemed to have notice of all matters contained in the document affecting the transfer within s 77(7)`
                 `the issuer demands assurance additional to that specified in section 77 for a purpose other than that specified in subsection 77(4)`
                 `the issuer obtains a copy of a will, trust or partnership agreement, by-law or similar document`
         AND `the matters contained in the document include an adverse claim`)

§§ `s 78(2) Discharge of duty`

-- Any reasonable means discharges the duty, "including" a notice sent by registered mail to the address the
-- claimant furnished (or, if none, to the claimant's residence or regular place of business) saying that a
-- security has been presented for transfer by a named person and that the transfer will be registered unless,
-- within thirty days from the date of mailing, either the issuer is served with a restraining order or other
-- order of a court, or is provided with an indemnity bond sufficient in the issuer's judgment. The mailed
-- notice route is read as discharging the duty when the thirty days have passed with neither (fork F-P7-10).
-- src:1051 | Discharge of duty
-- src:1052 | (2) An issuer may discharge a duty of inquiry by any reasonable means, including notifying an adverse claimant by registered mail sent to the address furnished by the claimant or, if no such address has been furnished, to the claimant’s residence or regular place of business, that a security has been presented for registration of transfer by a named person, and that the transfer will be registered unless within thirty days from the date of mailing the notice either
-- src:1053 | (a) the issuer is served with a restraining order or other order of a court; or
-- src:1054 | (b) the issuer is provided with an indemnity bond sufficient in the issuer’s judgment to protect the issuer and any registrar, transfer agent or other agent or mandatary of the issuer from any loss that may be incurred by any of them as a result of complying with the adverse claim.
@ref CBCA s 78(2) (src:1051-1054)
GIVEN `the issuer used another reasonable means to discharge the duty of inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the issuer notified the adverse claimant by registered mail sent to the address furnished by the claimant or, if none, to the claimant's residence or regular place of business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice stated that a security has been presented for registration of transfer by a named person and that the transfer will be registered unless within thirty days from the date of mailing the issuer is served with a restraining order or other order of a court or is provided with a sufficient indemnity bond` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of mailing` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
      `the date the issuer was served with a restraining order or other order of a court, if it was` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date the issuer was provided with an indemnity bond sufficient in its judgment, if it was` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the issuer has discharged the duty of inquiry within s 78(2)` MEANS
        `the issuer used another reasonable means to discharge the duty of inquiry`
    OR  (    `the issuer notified the adverse claimant by registered mail sent to the address furnished by the claimant or, if none, to the claimant's residence or regular place of business`
         AND `the notice stated that a security has been presented for registration of transfer by a named person and that the transfer will be registered unless within thirty days from the date of mailing the issuer is served with a restraining order or other order of a court or is provided with a sufficient indemnity bond`
         AND `the day asked about` GREATER THAN (`the last day of` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 30, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `counted from` `the date of mailing`)
         AND (NOT `an event happened within thirty days of mailing` `the date of mailing` `the date the issuer was served with a restraining order or other order of a court, if it was`)
         AND (NOT `an event happened within thirty days of mailing` `the date of mailing` `the date the issuer was provided with an indemnity bond sufficient in its judgment, if it was`))
    WHERE
        `an event happened within thirty days of mailing` mailed event MEANS
            CONSIDER event
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST d THEN `done within the time limit` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 30, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) mailed d

-- The two results above, as the other rules take them.
-- src:1048 | 78 (1) An issuer to whom a security is presented for registration has a duty to inquire into adverse claims if
-- src:1049 | (a) written notice of an adverse claim has been received at a time and in a manner that affords the issuer a reasonable opportunity to act on it before the issue of a new, reissued or re-registered security and the notice discloses the name and address of the claimant, the registered owner and the issue of which the security is a part; or
-- src:1050 | (b) the issuer is deemed to have notice of an adverse claim from a document that it obtained under subsection 77(7).
-- src:1051 | Discharge of duty
-- src:1052 | (2) An issuer may discharge a duty of inquiry by any reasonable means, including notifying an adverse claimant by registered mail sent to the address furnished by the claimant or, if no such address has been furnished, to the claimant’s residence or regular place of business, that a security has been presented for registration of transfer by a named person, and that the transfer will be registered unless within thirty days from the date of mailing the notice either
-- src:1053 | (a) the issuer is served with a restraining order or other order of a court; or
-- src:1054 | (b) the issuer is provided with an indemnity bond sufficient in the issuer’s judgment to protect the issuer and any registrar, transfer agent or other agent or mandatary of the issuer from any loss that may be incurred by any of them as a result of complying with the adverse claim.
@ref CBCA s 78(1)-(2) (src:1048-1054)
GIVEN `the issuer has a duty to inquire into adverse claims` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the issuer has discharged any duty to inquire into adverse claims` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the issuer had no duty to inquire into adverse claims or had discharged any such duty within s 78(1)` MEANS
        (NOT `the issuer has a duty to inquire into adverse claims`)
    OR  `the issuer has discharged any duty to inquire into adverse claims`

§§ `s 78(3) Inquiry into adverse claims`

-- "Unless an issuer is deemed to have notice ... under 77(7) or has received notice under subsection (1)":
-- that is, unless the issuer has a duty under s 78(1). The first input is the result of `the person is an
-- appropriate person within s 65(1)` in cb2-part7-endorsement.l4.
-- src:1055 | Inquiry into adverse claims
-- src:1056 | (3) Unless an issuer is deemed to have notice of an adverse claim from a document that it obtained under subsection 77(7) or has received notice of an adverse claim under subsection (1), if a security presented for registration is endorsed by the appropriate person as defined in section 65, the issuer has no duty to inquire into adverse claims, and in particular,
@ref CBCA s 78(3) (src:1055-1056)
GIVEN `the security presented for registration is endorsed by the appropriate person as defined in section 65` IS A BOOLEAN
      `written notice of an adverse claim has been received at a time and in a manner that affords the issuer a reasonable opportunity to act on it before the issue of a new, reissued or re-registered security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice discloses the name and address of the claimant, the registered owner and the issue of which the security is a part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the written notice was received` IS A DATE
      `the date the written notice was last renewed in writing, if it was` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
      `the issuer demands assurance additional to that specified in section 77 for a purpose other than that specified in subsection 77(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the issuer obtains a copy of a will, trust or partnership agreement, by-law or similar document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matters contained in the document include an adverse claim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the issuer has no duty to inquire into adverse claims within s 78(3)` MEANS
        `the security presented for registration is endorsed by the appropriate person as defined in section 65`
    AND (NOT `the issuer has a duty to inquire into adverse claims within s 78(1)`
                 `written notice of an adverse claim has been received at a time and in a manner that affords the issuer a reasonable opportunity to act on it before the issue of a new, reissued or re-registered security`
                 `the notice discloses the name and address of the claimant, the registered owner and the issue of which the security is a part`
                 `the date the written notice was received`
                 `the date the written notice was last renewed in writing, if it was`
                 `the day asked about`
                 `the issuer demands assurance additional to that specified in section 77 for a purpose other than that specified in subsection 77(4)`
                 `the issuer obtains a copy of a will, trust or partnership agreement, by-law or similar document`
                 `the matters contained in the document include an adverse claim`)

-- Paragraphs (a) to (c) are consequences "in particular" of the opening words; each takes the result of the
-- rule above as its first input (that rule asks nine facts).
-- src:1057 | (a) an issuer registering a security in the name of a person who is a fiduciary or who is described as a fiduciary is not bound to inquire into the existence, extent or correct description of the fiduciary relationship and thereafter the issuer may assume without inquiry that the newly registered owner continues to be the fiduciary until the issuer receives written notice that the fiduciary is no longer acting as such with respect to the particular security;
@ref CBCA s 78(3)(a) (src:1057)
GIVEN `the issuer has no duty to inquire into adverse claims under the opening words of subsection 78(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the issuer registers the security in the name of a person who is a fiduciary or who is described as a fiduciary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the issuer is bound to inquire into the existence, extent or correct description of the fiduciary relationship within s 78(3)(a)` MEANS
    IF     `the issuer has no duty to inquire into adverse claims under the opening words of subsection 78(3)`
       AND `the issuer registers the security in the name of a person who is a fiduciary or who is described as a fiduciary`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1057 | (a) an issuer registering a security in the name of a person who is a fiduciary or who is described as a fiduciary is not bound to inquire into the existence, extent or correct description of the fiduciary relationship and thereafter the issuer may assume without inquiry that the newly registered owner continues to be the fiduciary until the issuer receives written notice that the fiduciary is no longer acting as such with respect to the particular security;
@ref CBCA s 78(3)(a) (src:1057)
GIVEN `the issuer has no duty to inquire into adverse claims under the opening words of subsection 78(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the issuer registered the security in the name of a person who is a fiduciary or who is described as a fiduciary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the issuer has received written notice that the fiduciary is no longer acting as such with respect to the particular security` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the issuer may assume without inquiry that the newly registered owner continues to be the fiduciary within s 78(3)(a)` MEANS
        `the issuer has no duty to inquire into adverse claims under the opening words of subsection 78(3)`
    AND `the issuer registered the security in the name of a person who is a fiduciary or who is described as a fiduciary`
    AND (NOT `the issuer has received written notice that the fiduciary is no longer acting as such with respect to the particular security`)

-- src:1058 | (b) an issuer registering transfer on an endorsement by a fiduciary has no duty to inquire whether the transfer is made in compliance with the document or with the law of the jurisdiction governing the fiduciary relationship; and
@ref CBCA s 78(3)(b) (src:1058)
GIVEN `the issuer has no duty to inquire into adverse claims under the opening words of subsection 78(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the issuer registers the transfer on an endorsement by a fiduciary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the issuer has no duty to inquire whether the transfer complies with the document or the governing law within s 78(3)(b)` MEANS
        `the issuer has no duty to inquire into adverse claims under the opening words of subsection 78(3)`
    AND `the issuer registers the transfer on an endorsement by a fiduciary`

-- src:1059 | (c) an issuer is deemed not to have notice of the contents of any court record or any registered document even if the record or document is in the issuer’s possession and even if the transfer is made on the endorsement of a fiduciary to the fiduciary or the fiduciary’s nominee.
@ref CBCA s 78(3)(c) (src:1059)
GIVEN `the issuer has no duty to inquire into adverse claims under the opening words of subsection 78(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is a court record or a registered document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the issuer is deemed not to have notice of the contents of the record or document within s 78(3)(c)` MEANS
        `the issuer has no duty to inquire into adverse claims under the opening words of subsection 78(3)`
    AND `the document is a court record or a registered document`

§ `s 79 Limitation of issuer's liability`

§§ `s 79(1) Limitation of issuer's liability`

-- Subject to any applicable law relating to the collection of taxes.
-- src:1062 | Limitation of issuer’s liability
-- src:1063 | 79 (1) Subject to any applicable law relating to the collection of taxes, the issuer is not liable to the owner or any other person who incurs a loss as a result of the registration of a transfer of a security if
-- src:1064 | (a) the necessary endorsements were on or with the security; and
-- src:1065 | (b) the issuer had no duty to inquire into adverse claims or had discharged any such duty.
@ref CBCA s 79(1) (src:1062-1065)
GIVEN `the necessary endorsements were on or with the security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the issuer has a duty to inquire into adverse claims` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the issuer has discharged any duty to inquire into adverse claims` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an applicable law relating to the collection of taxes makes the issuer liable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the issuer is not liable for loss resulting from the registration within s 79(1)` MEANS
        `the necessary endorsements were on or with the security`
    AND `the issuer had no duty to inquire into adverse claims or had discharged any such duty within s 78(1)`
            `the issuer has a duty to inquire into adverse claims`
            `the issuer has discharged any duty to inquire into adverse claims`
    AND (NOT `an applicable law relating to the collection of taxes makes the issuer liable`)

§§ `s 79(2) Duty of issuer in default`

-- (a) is s 79(1), composed with its four inputs. (b) is s 80(1), composed with its three inputs. (c) overissue
-- is s 52(1), in cb2-part7-registers.l4: a plain input.
-- src:1066 | Duty of issuer in default
-- src:1067 | (2) If an issuer has registered a transfer of a security to a person not entitled to it, the issuer shall on demand deliver a like security to the owner unless
-- src:1068 | (a) subsection (1) applies;
-- src:1069 | (b) the owner is precluded by subsection 80(1) from asserting any claim; or
-- src:1070 | (c) the delivery would result in overissue, in which case the issuer’s liability is governed by section 52.
@ref CBCA s 79(2) (src:1066-1070)
GIVEN `the issuer has registered a transfer of the security to a person not entitled to it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the owner demands delivery of a like security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the necessary endorsements were on or with the security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the issuer has a duty to inquire into adverse claims` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the issuer has discharged any duty to inquire into adverse claims` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an applicable law relating to the collection of taxes makes the issuer liable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the security has been lost, apparently destroyed or wrongfully taken` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the owner fails to notify the issuer by written notice of an adverse claim within a reasonable time after discovering the loss, destruction or taking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the issuer registered a transfer of the security before receiving such notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the delivery would result in overissue` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the issuer must deliver a like security to the owner on demand within s 79(2)` MEANS
        `the issuer has registered a transfer of the security to a person not entitled to it`
    AND `the owner demands delivery of a like security`
    AND (NOT `the issuer is not liable for loss resulting from the registration within s 79(1)`
                 `the necessary endorsements were on or with the security`
                 `the issuer has a duty to inquire into adverse claims`
                 `the issuer has discharged any duty to inquire into adverse claims`
                 `an applicable law relating to the collection of taxes makes the issuer liable`)
    AND (NOT `the owner is precluded from asserting against the issuer any claim to a new security within s 80(1)`
                 `the security has been lost, apparently destroyed or wrongfully taken`
                 `the owner fails to notify the issuer by written notice of an adverse claim within a reasonable time after discovering the loss, destruction or taking`
                 `the issuer registered a transfer of the security before receiving such notice`)
    AND (NOT `the delivery would result in overissue`)

-- src:1066 | Duty of issuer in default
-- src:1067 | (2) If an issuer has registered a transfer of a security to a person not entitled to it, the issuer shall on demand deliver a like security to the owner unless
-- src:1068 | (a) subsection (1) applies;
-- src:1069 | (b) the owner is precluded by subsection 80(1) from asserting any claim; or
-- src:1070 | (c) the delivery would result in overissue, in which case the issuer’s liability is governed by section 52.
@ref CBCA s 79(2) (src:1066-1070)
GIVEN `the issuer has registered a transfer of the security to a person not entitled to it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the owner demands delivery of a like security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the delivery would result in overissue` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the issuer's liability is governed by section 52 within s 79(2)` MEANS
        `the issuer has registered a transfer of the security to a person not entitled to it`
    AND `the owner demands delivery of a like security`
    AND `the delivery would result in overissue`

§ `s 80 Notice of lost or stolen security`

§§ `s 80(1) Notice of lost or stolen security`

-- src:1071 | Notice of lost or stolen security
-- src:1072 | 80 (1) Where a security has been lost, apparently destroyed or wrongfully taken, and the owner fails to notify the issuer of that fact by giving the issuer written notice of an adverse claim within a reasonable time after discovering the loss, destruction or taking and if the issuer has registered a transfer of the security before receiving such notice, the owner is precluded from asserting against the issuer any claim to a new security.
@ref CBCA s 80(1) (src:1071-1072)
GIVEN `the security has been lost, apparently destroyed or wrongfully taken` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the owner fails to notify the issuer by written notice of an adverse claim within a reasonable time after discovering the loss, destruction or taking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the issuer registered a transfer of the security before receiving such notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the owner is precluded from asserting against the issuer any claim to a new security within s 80(1)` MEANS
        `the security has been lost, apparently destroyed or wrongfully taken`
    AND `the owner fails to notify the issuer by written notice of an adverse claim within a reasonable time after discovering the loss, destruction or taking`
    AND `the issuer registered a transfer of the security before receiving such notice`

§§ `s 80(2) Duty of issuer to issue a new security`

-- src:1073 | Duty of issuer to issue a new security
-- src:1074 | (2) Where the owner of a security claims that the security has been lost, destroyed or wrongfully taken, the issuer shall issue a new security in place of the original security if the owner
-- src:1075 | (a) so requests before the issuer has notice that the security has been acquired by a bona fide purchaser;
-- src:1076 | (b) furnishes the issuer with a sufficient indemnity bond; and
-- src:1077 | (c) satisfies any other reasonable requirements imposed by the issuer.
@ref CBCA s 80(2) (src:1073-1077)
GIVEN `the owner claims that the security has been lost, destroyed or wrongfully taken` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the owner requests a new security before the issuer has notice that the security has been acquired by a bona fide purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the owner furnishes the issuer with a sufficient indemnity bond` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the owner satisfies any other reasonable requirements imposed by the issuer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the issuer must issue a new security in place of the original within s 80(2)` MEANS
        `the owner claims that the security has been lost, destroyed or wrongfully taken`
    AND `the owner requests a new security before the issuer has notice that the security has been acquired by a bona fide purchaser`
    AND `the owner furnishes the issuer with a sufficient indemnity bond`
    AND `the owner satisfies any other reasonable requirements imposed by the issuer`

§§ `s 80(3) Duty to register transfer`

-- src:1078 | Duty to register transfer
-- src:1079 | (3) If, after the issue of a new security under subsection (2), a bona fide purchaser of the original security presents the original security for registration of transfer, the issuer shall register the transfer unless registration would result in overissue, in which case the issuer’s liability is governed by section 52.
@ref CBCA s 80(3) (src:1078-1079)
GIVEN `the issuer issued a new security under subsection 80(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a bona fide purchaser of the original security presents it for registration of transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `registration would result in overissue` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the issuer must register the transfer presented by the bona fide purchaser of the original within s 80(3)` MEANS
        `the issuer issued a new security under subsection 80(2)`
    AND `a bona fide purchaser of the original security presents it for registration of transfer`
    AND (NOT `registration would result in overissue`)

-- src:1078 | Duty to register transfer
-- src:1079 | (3) If, after the issue of a new security under subsection (2), a bona fide purchaser of the original security presents the original security for registration of transfer, the issuer shall register the transfer unless registration would result in overissue, in which case the issuer’s liability is governed by section 52.
@ref CBCA s 80(3) (src:1078-1079)
GIVEN `the issuer issued a new security under subsection 80(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a bona fide purchaser of the original security presents it for registration of transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `registration would result in overissue` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the issuer's liability is governed by section 52 within s 80(3)` MEANS
        `the issuer issued a new security under subsection 80(2)`
    AND `a bona fide purchaser of the original security presents it for registration of transfer`
    AND `registration would result in overissue`

§§ `s 80(4) Right of issuer to recover`

-- src:1080 | Right of issuer to recover
-- src:1081 | (4) In addition to any rights on an indemnity bond, the issuer may recover a new security issued under subsection (2) from the person to whom it was issued or anyone taking under the person other than a bona fide purchaser.
@ref CBCA s 80(4) (src:1080-1081)
GIVEN `the issuer issued a new security under subsection 80(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party is the person to whom the new security was issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party takes under the person to whom the new security was issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party is a bona fide purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the issuer may recover the new security from the party within s 80(4)` MEANS
        `the issuer issued a new security under subsection 80(2)`
    AND (   `the party is the person to whom the new security was issued`
         OR (    `the party takes under the person to whom the new security was issued`
             AND (NOT `the party is a bona fide purchaser`)))

§ `s 81 Rights and obligations of agents`

§§ `s 81(1) Rights and obligations`

-- src:1082 | Rights and obligations
-- src:1083 | 81 (1) An authenticating trustee, registrar, transfer agent or other agent or mandatary of an issuer has, in respect of the issue, registration of transfer and cancellation of a security of the issuer,
-- src:1084 | (a) a duty to the issuer to exercise good faith and reasonable diligence; and
-- src:1085 | (b) the same obligations to the holder or owner of a security and the same rights, privileges and immunities as the issuer.
@ref CBCA s 81(1) (src:1082-1085)
GIVEN `the person is an authenticating trustee, registrar, transfer agent or other agent or mandatary of an issuer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is the issue, registration of transfer or cancellation of a security of the issuer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the agent owes the issuer a duty to exercise good faith and reasonable diligence within s 81(1)` MEANS
        `the person is an authenticating trustee, registrar, transfer agent or other agent or mandatary of an issuer`
    AND `the matter is the issue, registration of transfer or cancellation of a security of the issuer`

-- src:1082 | Rights and obligations
-- src:1083 | 81 (1) An authenticating trustee, registrar, transfer agent or other agent or mandatary of an issuer has, in respect of the issue, registration of transfer and cancellation of a security of the issuer,
-- src:1084 | (a) a duty to the issuer to exercise good faith and reasonable diligence; and
-- src:1085 | (b) the same obligations to the holder or owner of a security and the same rights, privileges and immunities as the issuer.
@ref CBCA s 81(1) (src:1082-1085)
GIVEN `the person is an authenticating trustee, registrar, transfer agent or other agent or mandatary of an issuer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is the issue, registration of transfer or cancellation of a security of the issuer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the agent has the same obligations, rights, privileges and immunities as the issuer within s 81(1)` MEANS
        `the person is an authenticating trustee, registrar, transfer agent or other agent or mandatary of an issuer`
    AND `the matter is the issue, registration of transfer or cancellation of a security of the issuer`

§§ `s 81(2) Notice to agent or mandatary`

-- src:1086 | Notice to agent or mandatary
-- src:1087 | (2) Notice to an authenticating trustee, registrar, transfer agent or other agent or mandatary of an issuer is notice to the issuer with respect to the functions performed by the agent or mandatary.
@ref CBCA s 81(2) (src:1086-1087)
GIVEN `the notice is given to an authenticating trustee, registrar, transfer agent or other agent or mandatary of an issuer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice relates to the functions performed by the agent or mandatary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`notice to the agent or mandatary is notice to the issuer within s 81(2)` MEANS
        `the notice is given to an authenticating trustee, registrar, transfer agent or other agent or mandatary of an issuer`
    AND `the notice relates to the functions performed by the agent or mandatary`
